   "text": "I read the structure as a macrocycle and wrote it as SMILES by tracing around the ring, then assigned stereochemistry from the wedges and hashes.\n\n**Ring, traced from the proline:**\n1. D-proline (hashed bond to the ring CH2, R) acylated on its ring nitrogen by the carbonyl of N-methyl-phenylalanine, which closes the macrocycle.\n2. The proline carbonyl joins N-methyl-L-leucine (wedged isobutyl, S).\n3. The leucine carbonyl joins an N-methyl nitrogen, followed by CH2\u2013CH=CH\u2013C(=O)\u2013O. This double bond is drawn wavy, so I gave it no geometry.\n4. Next come O\u2013CH2\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013C(=O)\u2013C(=O), a dimethyl \u03b1-ketoamide that ends on the nitrogen of a piperidine.\n5. The piperidine is L-pipecolic acid (wedge, S). Its carboxyl forms an ester with the benzylic carbon (hashed bond, R).\n6. That benzylic carbon carries a CH2CH2 chain to a 3,4-dimethoxyphenyl group and sits on a meta-substituted benzene.\n7. The benzene bears NH\u2013C(=O)CH2CH2C(=O)\u2013NH, a succinamide linker, attached to L-aspartic acid tert-butyl ester (S).\n8. The aspartate carbonyl joins N-methyl-L-phenylalanine (S), whose carbonyl closes back onto the proline nitrogen.\n\nI worked out each @/@@ by assigning CIP priorities from the drawn wedge or hash and matching them to the neighbour order in the SMILES.\n\nSMILES: N19CCC[C@@H]1C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N(C)CC=CC(=O)OCC(C)(C)C(=O)C(=O)N2CCCC[C@H]2C(=O)O[C@H](CCc3ccc(OC)c(OC)c3)c3cccc(c3)NC(=O)CCC(=O)N[C@@H](CC(=O)OC(C)(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](Cc3ccccc3)C9=O"
